rchy reveals that the Stacking Ensemble achieved the highest performance with an $R^2$ of 0.97055, surpassing the Multiple Linear Regression (MLR) baseline of 0.96990. This victory was achieved through a strategic weighting process where the meta-learner assigned 38.5% of the influence to Support Vector Regression (SVR) for its kernel pattern recognition, 27.7% to XGBoost for non-linear residuals, 18.3% to Ridge for stabilization, and 16.5% to the original MLR for its linear foundation.We can see several key findings that are critical for the thesis. First, the performance victory was consistent, with the Stacking Ensemble outperforming all individual models and winning in four out of five cross-validation folds. Second, the ensemble represents a \"Goldilocks\" solution; it maintains a high degree of interpretability while achieving superior accuracy that individual \"black box\" models could not reach on their own. Finally, the training efficiency was notable, with the entire ensemble fitting in approximately 8 seconds, proving that high-level predictive power does not require prohibitive computational costs.Modelling the final project repository, all necessary assets have been successfully generated and stored. This includes the finalized comparison figures, summary tables, and the serialized champion model file, 06_stacking_ensemble.pkl. With these outputs secured, we are now ready to proceed to the final evaluation stage. This will involve training the stacking model on the complete training set and performing a single, definitive evaluation against the 97 unseen teachers in the test set to finalize the metrics for your thesis."],"metadata":{"id":"Y2f-GiphH1S-"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"PAj8gpeUPbXv"}}]}